WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.825 --> 00:00:14.465
Students write short reflections and goals in their lessons. Fixer Nation checks that writing, and if something serious comes up, an alert email goes out. In this video you'll choose who receives those emails at your school.

2
00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:19.916
Open the Organization page, and scroll down to Safety Alert Recipients.

3
00:00:20.418 --> 00:00:34.138
Type the email address of someone who should be told, such as a counselor or an assistant principal. Use an address that someone checks every day. You can also add a label, like School counselor, to remind you who it is.

4
00:00:34.639 --> 00:00:48.779
The category menu lets you choose which kind of alert this person receives. Leave it on all categories, and they get every alert. That's the catch-all, and it's a good idea to always have one, so no alert falls through the cracks.

5
00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:52.301
Select Add, and the person appears in the list.

6
00:00:52.801 --> 00:01:03.201
To send one kind of alert to someone else, add another person, and choose a category first. Here, the assistant principal will only receive alerts about bullying.

7
00:01:03.702 --> 00:01:08.962
To stop someone receiving alerts, select Remove beside their name, and confirm.

8
00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:24.493
The rest of this page shows your license details, such as your school domain, plan, seats, and end date. It also lists your co-administrators. Those are read only here. To add or change an administrator, contact us.

9
00:01:24.993 --> 00:01:30.003
Read only administrators can see this page, but can't change the recipients.
